From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: a523 8080 CPU-IF - complete vblank/flip from TRI_FINISH

===========================================================================
CANDIDATE - drafted + BUILD-VERIFIED 2026-10-15. HW test still pending.
Apply AFTER kernel/harvest-sun55i-de/drm-display-provisional.patch, against the
post-solve sun4i_tcon.c:

    patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=3 < kernel/harvest-sun55i-de/vblank-tri-finish.candidate.patch

then rebuild sun4i-tcon.ko (vermagic 7.3.0-rc7-dirty), deploy, and test per
docs/DISPLAY-VBLANK-ANALYSIS.md.

Verified: applies clean (offset located) AND builds in a full
`make Image modules dtbs` on v7.3-rc7 (EXIT 0, complete Module.symvers, no
modpost errors; sun4i-tcon.ko carries the fix). NOT yet HW-tested - does it
actually clear the flip_done timeouts and let fbcon/apps animate on the panel.
Now part of assemble-7.3.sh (step 1b).
===========================================================================

In 8080 MIPI-DSI CPU-interface mode the A523 TCON reports a completed frame via
TCON0_TRI_FINISH, and VBLANK_INT never fires. sun4i_tcon_handler() only completes
DRM's vblank/page-flip on VBLANK_INT, so drm_crtc_handle_vblank() is never called:
every atomic commit's flip_done then times out (10 s), the panel holds a single
frame (greyish, CRT-lines), and boot stalls while fbcon/agetty commits block.

The TRI_FINISH branch already runs the per-frame CPU-IF re-arm (gated on
a523_stock_trigger). Drive the vblank/flip completion from it too - signalling
the just-finished frame before arming the next push - so flip_done completes once
per pushed frame and DRM can actually drive updates.

(vblank is already registered/on for this CRTC: sun4i_crtc's atomic enable/disable
call drm_crtc_vblank_on()/_off(), and enable_vblank arms TRI_FINISH_ENABLE.)

Not-yet-verified (see the doc): no double-count if VBLANK_INT ever also fires;
per-frame handle_vblank keeps DRM's vblank timestamp/seqno sane; behaviour under
retrig_period_ms slow-refresh (flip_done then completes at that slower rate).

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)
Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
@@ -1268,6 +1268,16 @@ static irqreturn_t sun4i_tcon_handler(int irq, void *private)
 	 */
 	if (a523_stock_trigger && !retrig_disable &&
 	    (status & SUN4I_TCON_GINT0_TCON0_TRI_FINISH_INT)) {
+		/*
+		 * 8080 CPU-IF reports a finished frame via TRI_FINISH, not
+		 * VBLANK_INT (which never fires here). Treat it as the per-frame
+		 * vblank/flip-complete, or every DRM atomic commit's flip_done
+		 * times out (10 s) and the panel holds a single frame. Signal the
+		 * finished frame before arming the next CPU-IF push.
+		 */
+		drm_crtc_handle_vblank(&scrtc->crtc);
+		sun4i_tcon_finish_page_flip(drm, scrtc);
+
 		WRITE_ONCE(tcon->retrig_last_finish, ktime_get());
 		/* slow-refresh mode paces from the hrtimer instead (retrig_period_ms) */
 		if (!retrig_period_ms)
